    "bubble_choice_description": "Create a site map for a local animal shelter web app.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/85b89e293c25c63f403dda52f141d880-Pasted Graphic 12.png",
    "project_template_level_name": "ai-generated-design-lesson8-level1-level1c-template_2026",
    "name_suffix": "_2026",
    "teacher_markdown": "## Teaching Tips:\r\n\r\nSince students are filling out a site map, the goal is to ensure their page titles actually reflect the user experience.\r\n\r\nHave students pretend to navigate the site as if they are a user.\r\n\r\nAsk: \"Can a user find a specific pet, view its profile, and get back to the Home page in three clicks or less?\" This helps them identify if their sublevel pages (like Dog Profile or Cat Profile) are too buried.",
